@node Top
@top Aquí (aqui.el) User Guide

Version: 0.0.1

Copyright © 2026 @w{Charles Y. Choi}

THIS PROJECT IS WIP@.

Aquí (@code{aqui.el}) is an Elisp library for updating the location for GNU Emacs. On macOS@comma{} Aquí can use the Shortcuts app to query its native OS location service for more accurate results than those provided by an internet service. That said@comma{} Aquí can use an internet service to obtain location information if Shortcuts is not available.

Aquí updates the following Emacs variables:

@itemize
@item
@code{calendar-latitude}
@item
@code{calendar-longitude}
@item
@code{calendar-location-name}
@end itemize

These values are primarily used by the built-in library @code{solar.el}@comma{} which provides the @code{sunrise-sunset} command. Other third party commands providing local weather (e.g. wttr) can take advantage of location updates.


If you enjoy using Aquí@comma{} please consider buying me a coffee to help support its development and maintenance.

