@node Install
@chapter Install

@cindex Install
@vindex aqui
@vindex aqui-source
@vindex aqui-map-provider

Aquí is planned to be available on MELPA for installation via @code{package-install} (TBD).

There should be no setup required as commands provided by @code{aqui.el} are auto-loaded via @code{package-install}.

@subsubheading macOS Shortcuts Support

If a high-accuracy location update on macOS is desired@comma{} then install the following iCloud Shortcut:

@itemize
@item
@uref{https://www.icloud.com/shortcuts/5199bce93e314120b4bb78f17406592e, iCloud Shortcut: Current Location JSON}
@end itemize

Ensure that Aquí uses this Shortcut by setting the value of the customizable variable @code{aqui-source} to ``Shortcuts'' (@code{:shortcuts})


@subsubheading Customization

Customize Aquí via the @code{customize-group} command:

@example
M-x customize-group aqui RET
@end example

From here you can customize the following variables:

@table @asis
@item @code{aqui-source}
Select where location data should be sourced from.

The following sources are supported:

@itemize
@item
Shortcuts (@code{:shortcuts})
@item
ip-api.com  (@code{:ip-api})
@end itemize
@end table


@table @asis
@item @code{aqui-map-provider}
Select which map provider to use (Apple@comma{} Google).
@end table

@node Usage
@chapter Usage

@cindex Usage
@vindex aqui
@vindex aqui-insert-location

The following commands are provided by Aquí:

@deffn Command aqui
Update current geographic location from @code{aqui-source}.

Given an location update@comma{} the following variables are run-time updated:

@itemize
@item
@code{calendar-latitude}
@item
@code{calendar-longitude}
@item
@code{calendar-location-name}
@end itemize

Use the command @code{aqui-customize-save-location-data} to persist these variables to a file.
@end deffn

@deffn Command aqui-insert-location &optional LOCATION
@itemize
@item
LOCATION: Location object
@end itemize
@end deffn

@deffn Command aqui-customize-save-location-data
Persist location data in calendar location variables.

The following variables are persisted given a location update.

@itemize
@item
@code{calendar-latitude}
@item
@code{calendar-longitude}
@item
@code{calendar-location-name}
@end itemize
@end deffn

